+Everything — development, testing and demos — runs against a **local Anvil fork of Base**.
+The fork is a full local copy of Base state, so the jar talks to the *real* USDC contract at its
+real address, and demo tips move *real* forked USDC between test identities. Nothing is ever
+broadcast to Base, so there is no real money at risk.
 
